@@ -153,6 +153,33 @@ The following directives are provided for module and class contents:
       Describe the location where the object is defined.  The default value is
       the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
 
+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias.  The directive can be used at module level or
+   inside a class, and its body can contain a description.  References to an
+   alias can use :rst:role:`py:type` (or the general :rst:role:`py:obj` role).
+
+   The optional ``canonical`` option describes the type represented by the
+   alias.  When supplied, this expression appears after the alias name and an
+   equals sign in the signature, and referenced types are cross-referenced.
+   Omitting it leaves the alias name in the signature.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical: represented type
+      :type: text
+
+      The represented type, parsed as a Python annotation and shown in the
+      signature after ``=``.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined.  The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
+.. rst:role:: py:type
+
+   Reference a type alias declared with :rst:dir:`py:type`.
+
 .. rst:directive:: .. py:exception:: name
                    .. py:exception:: name(parameters)
                    .. py:exception:: name[type parameters](parameters)
